{
  "comment": "The game's GroundEffectTypes table, vendored so a ground effect can be NAMED without a Path of Exile install. The GroundEffect component carries only a row index (+0x48); this turns it into the game's own name for the kind of ground, and the name of the buff that kind applies. WHY VENDORED WHEN THE INSTALL IS AUTHORITATIVE: without it the feature does nothing on a machine that is only replaying a recording - which is every machine this project's tests run on - so the resolution could not be tested at all, only its failure modes. GroundEffectTypeTable prefers the install and falls back to this, so a patch that adds rows is picked up on a real machine while a replay still gets names. A row this file does not know is reported as its number, never guessed. WHAT THE TABLE SETTLES: every one of the 53 rows is a real effect kind applying a real buff - Ignited Ground, Chilled Ground, Shocked Ground, Caustic Ground. There is no decorative row (26 is literally called Unused). So carrying a GroundEffect component means the game considers this one of its ground-effect kinds, which is the opposite of a conclusion this project briefly recorded after mis-reading a loading-screen area name as a hideout. See the GroundEffect comment in schema/poe2.offsets.json.",
  "source": "repoe-fork/dat-export, current/poe2/heuristics/csv/GroundEffectTypes.csv and BuffDefinitions.csv",
